1
00:00:00,029 --> 00:00:04,389
In Responder, open Shifts from the
navigation, then choose Today.

2
00:00:04,820 --> 00:00:10,609
Across the top are My Shifts, Calendar,
Trades, On Duty and Approvals.

3
00:00:11,050 --> 00:00:13,140
Start by reading the intended day card.

4
00:00:13,550 --> 00:00:17,409
Here, A Shift at Firehouse 51 runs from
eight in the morning

5
00:00:17,440 --> 00:00:18,780
until eight the next morning.

6
00:00:19,190 --> 00:00:22,729
The words next day matter when planning an
overnight handover.

7
00:00:23,159 --> 00:00:25,950
Assigned describes this schedule's
assignment mode.

8
00:00:26,370 --> 00:00:30,870
You are on identifies the signed-in
person's roster membership, and Fully

9
00:00:30,870 --> 00:00:33,159
staffed is the displayed coverage result.

10
00:00:33,309 --> 00:00:35,920
Use Search shifts to narrow the list.

11
00:00:36,329 --> 00:00:39,740
Entering Community leaves the Community
standby signup card.

12
00:00:40,169 --> 00:00:42,769
Read its date and its eight-to-noon time
range.

13
00:00:43,130 --> 00:00:46,679
This card shows Sign-up and Approval
required, while the current

14
00:00:46,679 --> 00:00:48,719
account already shows You are on.

15
00:00:49,040 --> 00:00:53,169
Those labels answer different questions:
how this shift is offered, whether

16
00:00:53,169 --> 00:00:57,150
approval is required, and whether this
person is already on its roster.

17
00:00:57,540 --> 00:01:00,609
Searching changes what you see in the
list; it does not

18
00:01:00,609 --> 00:01:02,070
change the saved assignment.

19
00:01:02,189 --> 00:01:04,689
Open the standby card to read its day
detail.

20
00:01:05,110 --> 00:01:08,810
The heading and date identify the selected
occurrence, and Scheduled

21
00:01:08,810 --> 00:01:10,750
for repeats its time range.

22
00:01:11,120 --> 00:01:14,290
The page explicitly says that sign-ups and
trades on this

23
00:01:14,290 --> 00:01:16,430
shift need supervisor approval.

24
00:01:16,849 --> 00:01:19,399
Read that rule before planning a coverage
change.

25
00:01:19,850 --> 00:01:24,590
Open needs shows Firehouse 51 as Filled,
with No role requirements

26
00:01:24,590 --> 00:01:25,780
for this particular day.

27
00:01:26,170 --> 00:01:29,440
Request trade and Add person are visible
actions here.

28
00:01:29,840 --> 00:01:33,860
This walkthrough is inspecting the saved
day, so neither action is submitted.

29
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:36,579
Scroll through Roster and compare the
person with the

30
00:01:36,579 --> 00:01:38,190
group and role beside them.

31
00:01:38,650 --> 00:01:43,569
Wallace Boden appears under Command with
Chief, while the Engine and Squad entries

32
00:01:43,619 --> 00:01:45,680
identify their own people and roles.

33
00:01:46,069 --> 00:01:49,770
The repeated Scheduled label describes the
saved roster source.

34
00:01:50,190 --> 00:01:52,959
Use these details to check that the people
and functions

35
00:01:52,959 --> 00:01:54,530
you expected are represented.

36
00:01:54,899 --> 00:01:58,399
Confirm actual availability and attendance
through your department's

37
00:01:58,399 --> 00:02:01,530
procedures before assigning work based on
this schedule.

38
00:02:01,719 --> 00:02:04,709
Return to the shift views and choose My
Shifts.

39
00:02:05,130 --> 00:02:09,700
Under Shifts I am on, the A Shift summary
shows its code, personnel

40
00:02:09,700 --> 00:02:14,549
count, group count, next displayed day,
rotation and Assigned label.

41
00:02:14,990 --> 00:02:18,819
Scroll to the standby summary to compare
its own code and time range.

42
00:02:19,210 --> 00:02:22,370
It shows Manual, Sign-up and Approval
required.

43
00:02:22,880 --> 00:02:26,220
Upcoming days begins a separate section
below these summaries.

44
00:02:26,610 --> 00:02:29,870
Keep the shift definition and the dated
occurrence distinct when

45
00:02:29,870 --> 00:02:31,630
checking which day you need to open.

46
00:02:31,810 --> 00:02:34,740
Choose Calendar to look beyond the current
day's list.

47
00:02:35,099 --> 00:02:39,010
The month heading establishes the period
you are reading, and the filter row

48
00:02:39,010 --> 00:02:41,820
offers All Shifts or an individual shift.

49
00:02:42,180 --> 00:02:47,589
Select Training, Academy signup practice,
then select the twenty-seventh of October.

50
00:02:47,979 --> 00:02:52,559
The legend identifies My shifts, Open
slots and Fully staffed.

51
00:02:52,930 --> 00:02:56,639
The selected date appears above its day
card, which shows the practice

52
00:02:56,639 --> 00:03:00,669
shift from one until three in the
afternoon with two open slots.

53
00:03:00,979 --> 00:03:05,390
This recorded date is historical; its
open-slot label does not establish

54
00:03:05,419 --> 00:03:07,050
a current signup opportunity.

55
00:03:07,229 --> 00:03:10,650
Open that practice day to read the actual
group requirements.

56
00:03:11,120 --> 00:03:15,700
Open needs shows Firehouse 51 with Open,
two, and a Chief

57
00:03:15,700 --> 00:03:17,580
requirement marked Needed, two.

58
00:03:18,220 --> 00:03:21,359
Below it, Roster says No one is on this
day yet.

59
00:03:21,899 --> 00:03:24,990
Compare the required function with the
saved roster before

60
00:03:24,990 --> 00:03:26,390
deciding how to fill a gap.

61
00:03:26,960 --> 00:03:31,089
Add person is visible, but this inspection
does not change the roster.

62
00:03:31,480 --> 00:03:34,839
Checking the dated requirement helps a
supervisor distinguish an

63
00:03:34,890 --> 00:03:38,659
uncovered function from a day that simply
has a familiar shift name.

64
00:03:38,870 --> 00:03:41,389
Return to the views and choose On Duty.

65
00:03:41,849 --> 00:03:45,370
A Shift shows ten on-duty entries in this
recorded state.

66
00:03:45,760 --> 00:03:49,709
Each entry gives a name, group and role,
an Until time and

67
00:03:49,709 --> 00:03:51,060
a Scheduled source label.

68
00:03:51,529 --> 00:03:54,529
Read the shift heading with the individual
row so you do not

69
00:03:54,529 --> 00:03:56,480
mix two overlapping schedules.

70
00:03:56,980 --> 00:04:00,099
This view makes the saved coverage picture
easier to review.

71
00:04:00,470 --> 00:04:04,199
Its Scheduled entries still need the
appropriate availability and attendance

72
00:04:04,199 --> 00:04:06,220
checks for your department's real work.

73
00:04:06,370 --> 00:04:09,020
Choose Trades to review the trade
workspace.

74
00:04:09,419 --> 00:04:13,570
This account currently shows No shift
trades, and explains that requests

75
00:04:13,570 --> 00:04:15,549
you send or receive appear here.

76
00:04:15,929 --> 00:04:17,500
Then choose Approvals.

77
00:04:17,849 --> 00:04:22,240
The recorded result is Nothing to approve,
with a note that sign-ups and trades

78
00:04:22,240 --> 00:04:24,260
waiting for your approval appear here.

79
00:04:24,649 --> 00:04:27,059
These are the current account's displayed
queues.

80
00:04:27,420 --> 00:04:31,619
An empty queue is not a completed approval
or a confirmed replacement.

81
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:35,690
Read the actual pending entry and its
result whenever your department

82
00:04:35,690 --> 00:04:37,270
performs those operations.

83
00:04:37,499 --> 00:04:42,369
Return to the intended day and recheck its
identity, hours, personal roster

84
00:04:42,369 --> 00:04:44,159
label and approval requirement.

85
00:04:44,630 --> 00:04:48,540
The same checks help community
paramedicine and mental health teams plan

86
00:04:48,570 --> 00:04:53,339
outreach coverage, search-and-rescue teams
review mission support, security companies

87
00:04:53,339 --> 00:04:58,009
check a staffed post, wildland contractors
plan crew coverage, and industrial

88
00:04:58,009 --> 00:05:00,599
response teams review an emergency roster.

89
00:05:01,060 --> 00:05:04,659
Fire and EMS departments can use them for
their own station coverage.

90
00:05:05,159 --> 00:05:09,230
Match your department's roles and dates,
investigate gaps, and verify

91
00:05:09,230 --> 00:05:12,910
the actual people before relying on a
schedule for a handover.

